    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.dag_to_branching - EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\":\n    {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.dag_to_branching.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.dag_to_branching()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: >-\n    Unfold a directed acyclic graph into a branching (forest) of its\n    root-to-leaf paths.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.dag_to_branching()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: >-\n    Unfold a directed acyclic graph into a branching (forest) of its\n    root-to-leaf paths.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.dag_to_branching()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: >-\n  Unfold a directed acyclic graph into a branching (forest) of its root-to-leaf\n  paths.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nUnfold a directed acyclic graph into a branching (forest) of its root-to-leaf paths.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L73578-L73694){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.dag_to_branching()\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![DAG to branching](../assets/graphs/dag-to-branching.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"Left: a diamond DAG in which A points to B and C, and both point to D (accent color). Right: dag_to_branching() unrolls every root-to-leaf path into a tree: A leads to A/B and A/C, and D, reached along both paths, appears twice, as A/B/D and A/C/D in the accent color. Each new node is labeled with its path, and the result is a branching.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nEvery path from a root (a node without incoming edges) to a leaf (a node without\noutgoing edges) becomes a path of the result, and paths that share a prefix share their\nnodes, so the result is a forest: the DAG \"unrolled\" so that no node has two parents.\nNodes reachable along several paths are duplicated, once per distinct path prefix. This\nturns a DAG into a tree for algorithms and visualizations that need one (a family tree\nwith shared ancestors drawn as a tree, a decision process, or a call graph expanded into\na call tree).\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Graph]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   A new directed forest. Each node is labeled with its path from the root, such as\n    `\"A/B/D\"`, and stores the ID of the original node in the attribute `\"source\"`.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If the graph is undirected or has a cycle.\n:::\n\n## Technical Notes {.doc-technical-notes}\n\nThe root-to-leaf paths are inserted into a prefix tree (trie), as in NetworkX's\n`dag_to_branching`. The result can be exponentially larger than the DAG, since the\nnumber of paths can grow exponentially.\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~is_branching`) \n\n:   Check that a directed graph is a forest of arborescences.\n\n[](`~all_topological_sorts`) \n\n:   Every topological ordering.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nIn a diamond, `D` is reached through `B` and through `C`, so it appears twice:\n\n::: {#7f40df63 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngraph = ec.Graph.from_edges(\n    [(\"A\", \"B\"), (\"A\", \"C\"), (\"B\", \"D\"), (\"C\", \"D\")], directed=True\n)\ntree = graph.dag_to_branching()\n\ntree.get_node_df().select(\"label\", \"source\"), tree.is_branching()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n(shape: (5, 2)\n ┌───────┬────────┐\n │ label ┆ source │\n │ ---   ┆ ---    │\n │ str   ┆ i64    │\n ╞═══════╪════════╡\n │ A     ┆ 1      │\n │ A/B   ┆ 2      │\n │ A/B/D ┆ 4      │\n │ A/C   ┆ 3      │\n │ A/C/D ┆ 4      │\n └───────┴────────┘,\n True)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Every chain of prerequisites\n\n`courses()` holds the courses of a made-up computer science program, with an arrow from\neach course to every course that requires it. Unfolding CS460 and the courses it needs\ngives a tree for each starting course, with a copy of CS460 at the end of each chain of\nprerequisites. There are four chains:\n\n::: {#9f4bb074 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ncourses = ec.courses()\nneeded = courses.subgraph(\n    [*courses.ancestors(\"CS460\"), courses.get_id_from_label(\"CS460\")]\n)\ntree = needed.dag_to_branching()\n\n[label for label in tree.get_node_df()[\"label\"]\n if label.endswith(\"CS460\")]\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n['CS101/CS102/CS201/CS360/CS460',\n 'CS101/CS201/CS360/CS460',\n 'MATH101/MATH102/MATH210/STAT201/CS360/CS460',\n 'MATH150/CS201/CS360/CS460']\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#6ee609a7 .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nlabels = tree.get_node_df()[\"label\"]\ntree.set_node_attrs(\n    \"course\", {label: label.rsplit(\"/\", 1)[-1] for label in labels}\n)\ntree.set_node_attrs(\n    \"depth\", {label: label.count(\"/\") for label in labels}\n)\ntree.layout_multipartite(subset_key=\"depth\").plot(\n    layout=\"pos\", label_by=\"course\", height=360,\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-high-contrast-light), html[theme=\"dark\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}</style><div class=\"ec-plot\" style=\"position:relative;width:fit-content;max-width:100%;margin:1em auto\">\n<style>.ec-plot > svg { display:block; max-width:100%; height:auto; }</style>\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"700\" height=\"360\" viewBox=\"4.3 14.0 684.4 352.0\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;\">\n<rect x=\"4.3\" y=\"14.0\" width=\"684.4\" height=\"352.0\" fill=\"var(--ect-3239c383)\"/>\n<g opaci